emain explicitly owned. Full original component/application retarget and removal duties remain retained.\n\nSecurity: Shared variants now validate fixed nested effects, inputs, uses, prepared results, sends, members, grants and references while explicitly preserving opaque request bodies, outcome evidence and owner-defined application data. Submission and founding refusal unions are separated. HTTP failure preserves an unknown submitted outcome and asks for retry of the same signed intent. Production authority/read ports deny by default. Replay's integrity mode checks canonical bytes, hashes, chain and signatures; full replay derives judgments while exposing grant, clock, anchor and outside-effect trusts. The two findings above are still required before the broad reply/bounded-reader claims can be accepted.\n\nSimplification: One fixed-shape implementation and one body reader reduce divergent validation. The remaining changes fit those shared primitives and the existing compact tables. The active/parked boundary is explicit; historical protocol and parked Room guides are replacement material, not active implementation authority. The delivery correctly qualifies the older/newer timings as different product scopes. Producer typecheck/205-test/~five-second claims are attribution only; no independent execution or comparable whole install/setup/edit-to-review wall/CPU tenfold result was obtained.\n\nNonblocking documentation: bytes README's opening calls every export pure and synchronous although takeBytes and within are asynchronous with timers/cancellation; qualify that introduction. Some derivation prose still calls adopted revision10 pending; refresh current authority labels while preserving historical reading. Temporary old bounds and entries-only accounting remain owned deviations, not new implementation guarantees.\n\nComplete ordinary coverage: all 157 current declared bodies were freshly read through EOF by delegated reviewers, including unchanged sources, tests